Proposed upstream fix — do not apply this to a production billing install
==========================================================================

This file is a proposal for FOSSBilling maintainers. Shipping it here does not
mean a billing server should apply it.

Applies to: FOSSBilling 0.8.x (checked against 0.8.9)

Why
---
`ServiceDomain\Service::syncWhois()` writes both dates unconditionally:

    $model->expires_at    = $this->formatRegistrarTimestamp($whois->getExpirationTime());
    $model->registered_at = $this->formatRegistrarTimestamp($whois->getRegistrationTime());

Registrar adapters that cannot report a creation date (Enom's `GetDomainInfo`
does not return one, and `_getD()` never populates
`Registrar_Domain::setRegistrationTime()`) hand back `null`, which is then
written over a date FOSSBilling already knew. Every cron sync therefore wipes
`service_domain.registered_at`.

A registrar adapter cannot fix this on its own: it never receives the stored
value, and it does not control what the core writes.

Patch
-----
--- a/src/modules/Servicedomain/Service.php
+++ b/src/modules/Servicedomain/Service.php
@@ -403,8 +403,17 @@
         $model->contact_phone = $contact->getTel();
         $model->details = serialize($whois);
-        $model->expires_at = $this->formatRegistrarTimestamp($whois->getExpirationTime());
-        $model->registered_at = $this->formatRegistrarTimestamp($whois->getRegistrationTime());
+        // Only overwrite a stored date when the registrar actually returned one.
+        // Registrars such as Enom do not expose a creation date, and writing null
+        // here would erase a date that was already known.
+        $expiresAt = $this->formatRegistrarTimestamp($whois->getExpirationTime());
+        if ($expiresAt !== null) {
+            $model->expires_at = $expiresAt;
+        }
+        $registeredAt = $this->formatRegistrarTimestamp($whois->getRegistrationTime());
+        if ($registeredAt !== null) {
+            $model->registered_at = $registeredAt;
+        }
         $model->synced_at = date('Y-m-d H:i:s');
         $model->updated_at = date('Y-m-d H:i:s');
         $this->di['db']->store($model);

Same idea for nameservers
-------------------------
`syncWhois()` never reads `$whois->getNs1()`…`getNs4()`, so an adapter cannot
report a delegation change. If you want panel-side nameserver changes to show
up in FOSSBilling, add after the contact block:

    foreach ([1, 2, 3, 4] as $slot) {
        $value = $whois->{'getNs' . $slot}();
        if (is_string($value) && $value !== '') {
            $model->{'ns' . $slot} = $value;
        }
    }

Note that `Model_ServiceDomain::$ns1`…`ns4` are written by
`updateNameservers()` on the FOSSBilling side, so only overwrite them when the
registrar returned a value.

Verification
------------
1. Register or import a domain, set `registered_at` in `service_domain`.
2. Run the domain sync (admin *Sync* or the cron task).
3. Before the patch: `registered_at` becomes `NULL`. After: it is unchanged
   when the registrar reports no creation date, and it is updated when the
   registrar does report one.
